(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "dossier.commoncrawl real live client" "non-authoritative web-presence enrichment, explicitly separate from governed registry facts")), (:adr/topic "isic-8291-commoncrawl-web-presence-enrichment"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607182200" "adr-2607182300" "adr-2607110400")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607182400-isic-8291-commoncrawl-web-presence-enrichment"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-18"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607182400: cloud-itonami-isic-8291 dossier -- real Common Crawl Index client, deliberately non-authoritative\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner suggestion: \\\"\u4ed6\u306b\u3082 commoncrawl \u3084\u516c\u958b\u60c5\u5831\u304b\u3089\u53ce\u96c6\u66f4\u65b0\u3059\u308b path \u3082\\\" -- naming Common Crawl / general public-info sources as an additional collection/update path alongside ADR-2607182200's official-registry work)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8291` (child commit `d190cf231a57`), west pin advance.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdded `dossier.commoncrawl` (keyless, JVM-only `.clj`, mirrors `dossier.companies-house`'s structure) as a real Common Crawl Index Server client. Unlike houjin-bangou (ADR-2607182200, blocked on a 2-4 week Application ID registration), Common Crawl needs no key at all -- **this module was exercised live against the real API in this session**, closing the \\\"not yet live-verified\\\" gap the houjin-bangou client still carries.\n\n### Deliberately kept OUT of the governed fact-basis system\n\n`dossier.facts`'s catalog exists specifically to name the ONLY sources the DisclosureGovernor will accept as citation for a company/official/relationship fact -- every existing entry (GLEIF, Companies House, SEC EDGAR, houjin-bangou) is a government/consortium-maintained authoritative registry. Common Crawl is a raw, unmoderated web crawl: it can confirm \\\"this URL had a page on this date\\\", never \\\"this is a real registered company\\\". This module therefore has **no `->company` mapper**, is **not added to `dossier.facts`'s catalog**, and is **not wired into `dossier.live-store`'s decorator chain** -- treating a crawl hit as registry-grade evidence would fabricate exactly the kind of authority this actor's governed design exists to prevent. `->enrichment` returns a shape with no `:id`/`:legal-name`/`:jurisdiction`, so it can never be mistaken for a dossier Company by a caller who mixes up mapper functions.\n\n### Real, load-bearing scope finding (live-verified, not assumed)\n\nThe real Common Crawl Index API is **URL-keyed only** -- querying without an exact `url=` parameter returns `{\\\"message\\\": \\\"The 'url' param is required\\\"}}`; there is no full-text/content search endpoint at all. This means the module is a **verification/enrichment tool for a domain you already have** (confirm a candidate company's website is real and when it was last crawled), never an **industry/keyword discovery mechanism** -- it cannot answer \\\"find employment agencies in Tokyo\\\". This is stated plainly in the ns docstring as a real limitation, not glossed over.\n\n### Bug caught by live verification\n\nCommon Crawl's real no-match response is **HTTP 404 WITH a real, parseable JSON body** (`{\\\"message\\\": \\\"No Captures found for: ...\\\"}}`), not a bare error page. The first implementation only parsed HTTP 200 responses, so every genuine no-match silently degraded to `nil` (\\\"transport failed, unknown\\\") instead of `[]` (\\\"confirmed absent from this crawl\\\") -- caught immediately by testing against a real nonexistent domain live, fixed, and now regression-tested with a fixture reproducing the exact 404-plus-JSON shape.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- cloud-itonami now has a genuinely live-verified, keyless enrichment tool alongside the (not-yet-verified) official-registry sources -- useful once a candidate company/domain is already known (from MHLW's licensed-agency search, ADR-2607182300, or houjin-bangou once its Application ID lands).\n- Does NOT solve prospect discovery-by-industry -- that gap remains open, and per this API's real shape, Common Crawl specifically cannot close it; MHLW's licensed-agency registry (already confirmed real and working, ADR-2607182300) remains the correctly-scoped discovery path for 7810's ICP.\n- Tests: 123/510 assertions green (was 113/492), clj-kondo clean.\n"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607182400: cloud-itonami-isic-8291 dossier -- real Common Crawl Index client, deliberately non-authoritative web-presence enrichment"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))